//? Title: Selective Kernels: Normalized Branch Choice and a Complete SKNet Fit
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Tensor attention modules expose how global context changes channel or branch weights.
We check the small module, complete network counts and gradients, then show every update
of the source-shaped compact CIFAR classifier with tensor Adam.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/sknet.cpp`.

> The method

A selective-kernel unit has two grouped 3×3/BN/ReLU branches, with dilation one and two.
Their SUM is globally averaged and reduced to max(C/r,L) through bias-free 1×1/BN/ReLU.
Two bias-free expansions give branch logits; a softmax across the TWO BRANCHES normalizes
weights per sample and channel. The output is the weighted branch sum. Independent sigmoids
would change that definition. Mathematically positive weights can underflow to zero
in floating arithmetic; the small support fixture uses .01 filters to avoid saturation. The dilated branch samples nine taps over 5×5 rather than using
a dense 5×5 kernel. Controlled positive inputs/filters expose branch-only derivative supports
at strides one and two; complete attention derivatives also flow through pooled selection.

SKNet-50 uses a ResNeXt 32×4d backbone, replacing each spatial filter with an SK unit, r=16
and L=32. Its full learned count is 27479784, adding 2450880 over ResNeXt-50. Grouped dilated
core kernels replace the source release's split/zero-expanded implementation, preserving counts
and connectivity. The quarter-width CIFAR network retains cardinality 32, group widths 1/2/4/8,
and all sixteen blocks. Its conv2 callback captures normalization options by value; diagnostic
state freezing must also freeze that callback's own update_stats setting.

The backbone retains all sixteen ResNet-50 bottlenecks (3/4/6/3). Each unit ends with a linear
1×1/BN, its attention gate, shortcut addition and ReLU. He-uniform bias-free convolution
filters use symmetric padding, and BN learns scale/shift with epsilon 1e-5. A global mean
and biased classifier finish the model. In grouped variants, the width is
floor(planes*base_width/64)*cardinality. Stage stride belongs either to the first 1×1 or to
the spatial filter; grouped layers and replacement hooks receive the actual spatial stride,
preventing double downsampling when it belongs to the first filter.

Full-width count/forward and backward probes below use 64-pixel inputs to bound computation;
they retain every block and channel but are not full-resolution ImageNet accuracy evaluations.
The backward probe freezes moving updates, shifts BN betas away from inactive ReLUs, and checks
every parameter gradient is finite. Its printed norm range does not guarantee every derivative
is nonzero for arbitrary data or gates. All numerical model/gradient computations use tensors.

The explicit fit uses the source's quarter-width CIFAR backbone: a 3×3 stride-one stem without
pooling, all sixteen blocks, stage stride on the 3×3 SK branches and original 32×32 images. It shows
8 batch-eight epochs (128 updates, kept short so the report builds quickly) on 128 fit/64
validation/64 official-test rows, tensor Adam(.001), explicit
kernel L2=.0001/2, padded crops/flips and paired learned/BN checkpoint selection by validation NLL.
All attention parameters participate in the optimizer. This bounded single-seed run differs
from the paper's ImageNet schedule and cannot establish attention accuracy superiority.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/sknet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/sknet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/sknet_concept.tikz > build/sknet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/sknet_concept.svg build/sknet_concept.dvi > build/sknet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
